416 0 obj
<<
/A 2455 0 R
/Alt (Flowchart of the GM Markov WOA method. It starts with Data collection and cleaning. If Ratio Test is passed, it proceeds to GM \(1,1\) Prediction, obtaining prediction results. Next, the residuals are calculated and divided into states. A Markov chain is used to predict the residual state, determining the interval. The weighted sum of upper and lower bounds serves as the predicted residual based on the residual state within a corresponding interval. This section is labeled GM \(1,1\)-Markov. The optimal weight is obtained with WOA, thus converting intervals into prediction residuals. This process is labeled as WOA Optimizes. The Markov chain also predicts the interval Residual State . Finally, different parameters weights correspond to different RMSE values. The optimal weight with the lowest RMSE is selected as the final result.)
/K 45
/P 37 0 R
/Pg 14 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
