539 0 obj
<<
/A 2577 0 R
/Alt (. This flowchart details the iterative process of the Whale Optimization Algorithm \(WOA\). It begins with initializing the whale population and calculating individual fitness to identify the best agent. A decision node checks whether the current iteration is less than the maximum iterations. If true, the algorithm updates parameters and uses three core mechanisms: Encircling Prey, Bubble-net Attack, and Search For Prey, to update each agent&#x02019;s position, then refreshes the global optimal solution. The loop continues until the stopping criterion is met, at which point the global best solution is returned.)
/K 27
/P 37 0 R
/Pg 17 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
