<<
/A 2638 0 R
/Alt (The six-panel line graph arranged in two rows of three shows Level Ratio on the vertical axis versus Year from 2015 to 2023 on the horizontal axis for various gas supply and user types. Panel one, Natural Gas Supply, shows Original Ratios fluctuating between the Lower Bound of 0.85 and Upper Bound of 1.05. Panel two, Natural Gas Users, shows Original Ratios fluctuating between 0.90 and 1.00, staying within the Lower Bound of 0.85 and Upper Bound of 1.05. Panel three, Artificial Gas Supply moved with c \(58.23\), shows Original Ratios fluctuating between 0.90 and 1.60, with Translated Ratios fluctuating between 1.00 and 1.20. Both stay within the Lower Bound of 0.80 and Upper Bound of 1.20. Panel four, Artificial Gas Users with c \(924.61\), shows Original Ratios fluctuating between 0.90 and 1.40, with Translated Ratios fluctuating between 0.95 and 1.20. Both stay within the Lower Bound of 0.90 and Upper Bound of 1.20. Panel five, LPG Supply with c \(207.61\), shows Original Ratios fluctuating between 0.90 and 1.20, with Translated Ratios fluctuating between 0.90 and 1.20. Both stay within the Lower Bound of 0.90 and Upper Bound of 1.20. Panel six, LPG Users, shows Original Ratios fluctuating between 0.90 and 1.10, staying within the Lower Bound of 0.85 and Upper Bound of 1.15.)
/K 100
/P 37 0 R
/Pg 19 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
