/A 2798 0 R
/Alt (- This bar graph compares the Root Mean Squared Error \(RMSE\) of five prediction models&#x02014;GM\(1,1\), ARIMA, GM&#x02013;Markov, PSO-GM&#x02013;Markov, and WOA-GM&#x02013;Markov&#x02014;across six gas datasets: NG Supply, NG Users, AG Supply, AG Users, LPG Supply, and LPG Users, using a logarithmic vertical axis to highlight differences. For NG Supply, RMSE values are 64.6, 169.8, 84.0, 61.4, and 61.3. For NG Users, values are 932.0, 18072, 551.9, 529.5, and 529.5. AG Supply shows values of 3.2, 18.8, 3.3, 3.3, and 3.3. AG Users has values of 66.5, 581.7, 73.8, 66.5, and 66.5. LPG Supply has values of 50.7, 350.9, 51.0, 50.4, and 50.4. For LPG Users, values are 220.3, 1030.7, 258.5, 220.3, and 220.3. ARIMA showed the highest RMSE overall, while WOA-GM&#x02013;Markov achieved the lowest RMSE most, outperforming both basic GM\(1,1\) and PSO-optimized GM&#x02013;Markov slightly, confirming its superior accuracy for small-sample gas data.)
